# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Qurus Next.js project.

## Implementation Details

### 1. Fetched Latest Documentation
- Retrieved the latest installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Confirmed the project uses Next.js App Router (based on the presence of `app/layout.tsx`)

### 2. Installed Package
- Added `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 to project dependencies
- Used npm (the project's package manager) to install the package
- Successfully updated package.json and package-lock.json

### 3. Configured Analytics Component
Modified `website/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body element, following Vercel's recommended placement
- Preserved all existing code structure, metadata, and styling

### 4. Verification Steps Completed
✓ Build verification: `npm run build` completed successfully
✓ Linter check: `npm run lint` passed with no errors
✓ TypeScript compilation: Passed without errors
✓ All routes generated successfully

## Files Modified
- `website/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component
- `website/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `website/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package dependencies

## Next Steps for User
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard:
   - Navigate to your project's Analytics tab
   - Click the "Enable" button in the header
2. Deploy the changes to Vercel
3. After deployment, verify setup by checking browser's Network tab for a request from `/<unique-path>/view` when visiting pages

## Technical Notes
- The Analytics component is framework-agnostic and will automatically track page views
- No additional configuration is required in the code
- Analytics data will appear in the Vercel dashboard once enabled and deployed
- The implementation follows Vercel's official Next.js App Router guidelines
